## 2. The ₹3,50,000 Kickback Machine: How Agents Weaponize the TUM Headline

Why have you heard so much about TUM's fees, but almost nothing about the hundreds of public universities that remain 100% free?

The answer comes down to one ruthless industry reality: **The Study Abroad Agent Commission Model.**

### The Consultant's Conflict of Interest
Public universities in Germany are funded by German taxpayers. Because they are government-subsidized, **they do not pay a single euro of commission to any educational agent or consultancy**. Whether you get into RWTH Aachen, TU Berlin, or TU Darmstadt, the agent makes **₹0** from the German government.

On the other hand, commercial private universities and unranked "business schools" operating private branch campuses in Berlin, Munich, Frankfurt, or Hamburg depend entirely on commissioned recruiters.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                       THE AGENT'S CONFLICT OF INTEREST                      │
├──────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 🇩🇪 Elite Public University (€0 Fees)  │ 🏢 Commercial Private School (€15k)  │
├──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤
│ • Tuition Fee: €0                    │ • Tuition Fee: €12,000 – €18,000/year│
│ • Global World Rank: Top 50–150      │ • Global World Rank: Unranked / Tier │
│ • Agent Commission: ₹0 (Zero)        │ • Agent Commission: 15% to 25%       │
│ • Post-Study Job Placement: 94%+     │ • Post-Study Job Placement: Low/Poor │
│ • Cost to Student: ₹0                │ • Cost to Student: ₹25L–₹35L Loan    │
│                                      │                                      │
│ ❌ AGENT LOSES PROFIT                │ 💰 AGENT EARNS ₹1.5L TO ₹3.5L CASH!  │
└──────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### The "Darr Ka Dhanda" (Fear Pitch) Exposed
When TUM announced its fees, unscrupulous consultants found their ultimate sales script. They sit down with anxious Indian parents in Kolhapur, Pune, or Delhi and say:

> *"Uncle, German government ne rules badal diye hain. Ab Germany me sab jagah fees lagti hai. Public universities me admission milna namumkin hai, aur ab wahan bhi lakho rupaye lag rahe hain. Isse achha hamare partner institute me admission lo—hum aapka 100% visa aur guaranteed seat karwa ke denge."*

**This is deliberate deception.** 

Students are pushed into private colleges charging **€12,000 to €18,000 per year (₹11 Lakhs to ₹16 Lakhs)** for degrees that German employers don't respect. Families take high-interest **13.5% unsecured NBFC education loans** of ₹35 Lakhs, trapping the student under a **₹55,000/month EMI** before they even graduate! (To understand how predatory agents manipulate admissions, read our detailed [Best Study Abroad Consultants in Kolhapur & Agent Scams Audit](/intelligence/best-study-abroad-overseas-education-consultants-kolhapur-scams-guide)).

