## 5. The 3-Step DAAD Self-Audit Protocol: How to Check Any Degree Yourself

Never take any consultant’s word for whether a course is free, chargeable, or secretly bilingual. You can verify any German degree in under 60 seconds using the official German government database:

### Step 1: Open the Official DAAD International Programs Database
Visit the official portal of the **German Academic Exchange Service**: [daad.de/international-programmes](https://www2.daad.de/deutschland/studienangebote/international-programmes/en/).

* In the search bar, select your **Course Type** (e.g., *Master's degree*).
* Select **Course Language**: Choose **"Only English"** (This is crucial to avoid the [Bilingual Degree Trap in Germany](/intelligence/the-bilingual-degree-trap-germany-hidden-language-requirements)).
* In the **Field of Study**, select your engineering, data science, or management domain.

### Step 2: Inspect the "Tuition Fees per Semester" Filter
Look at the left-hand sidebar filters under **"Tuition fees per semester"**:
* Select the checkbox: **"None"**.
* The database will instantly refresh, filtering out every single university that charges tuition fees.
* You will be presented with a verified list of hundreds of state-regulated, 100% free public programs.

### Step 3: Inspect the Specific Program Profile & Modulhandbuch
Click on any course from your shortlist:
* Navigate to the **"Overview"** tab and check the **"Tuition fees per semester in EUR"** field. It must state: **"None"**.
* Check the **"Semester contribution"** field to see the exact €150–€350 welfare fee.
* Verify the university type: It must say **"Public"** (*Staatliche Hochschule* or *Universität*). If it says "Private", close the tab immediately.

