## 6. How the Mathematics Changes Your Family Balance Sheet

Let’s look at the cold, hard numbers for a 2-year Master's in Computer Science or Mechanical Engineering:

| Parameter | Public University in Free State (e.g., RWTH Aachen) | TUM / Baden-Württemberg (Chargeable Public) | Private Commercial College (Agent Pitch) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Tuition Fee (2 Years)** | **₹0** | ₹6.0 Lakhs – ₹11.0 Lakhs | **₹24.0 Lakhs – ₹36.0 Lakhs** |
| **Semester Contributions (4 Sems)** | ~₹1.2 Lakhs *(Includes Transit)* | ~₹1.2 Lakhs | ~₹1.0 Lakhs |
| **Living Expenses (Blocked Account)** | ~₹23.0 Lakhs (€11,904/yr) | ~₹23.0 Lakhs | ~₹23.0 Lakhs |
| **Total Out-of-Pocket Expenditure** | **~₹24.2 Lakhs** | **~₹30.2 Lakhs – ₹35.2 Lakhs** | **~₹48.0 Lakhs – ₹60.0 Lakhs** |
| **Unsecured Student Loan Required** | ₹0 to ₹15 Lakhs (Minimal) | ₹15 Lakhs to ₹25 Lakhs | **₹40 Lakhs to ₹50 Lakhs (Severe Risk)** |
| **Monthly Loan EMI After Graduation** | **₹0 – ₹18,000** | ₹22,000 – ₹35,000 | **₹65,000 – ₹80,000 (10 Years!)** |
| **Industry Credibility & Placement** | **Elite Global Recognition** | Elite Global Recognition | Low / Tier-3 Resume Disqualification |

Notice the difference: By securing a public university in one of the 14 zero-tuition states, **you save ₹25 Lakhs to ₹35 Lakhs in pure debt**. 

That is money your parents do not have to borrow from an NBFC at 13.5% interest, and an EMI burden you will not have to drag around your neck when starting your career in Europe. (To understand why Europe's macroeconomic model beats the debt-traps of Canada and the UK, read our deep dive on [The Great Study Abroad Shift 2026: Why Continental Europe Won](/intelligence/the-macroeconomic-study-abroad-shift-2026-canada-uk-vs-europe)).

